               Wrapper CLasses
               ================
1.Wrapper classes in java are a group of 8 classes available in the package java.lang

2.They have their names resembling with the name of primitive datatypes

3.Their have very very imp uses and there are two uses.

a.For converting String representation of a value to its original type .

For ex: to convert "25" to 25 we will use this Wrapper class Integer and we will call its method parseInt()

====================================================================================================================


Wrapper class             |     Parse Method
                          |
1.Integer                 |   parseInt()
                          |
2.Double                  |   parseDouble
                          |
3.Float                   |   parseFloat()
                          |
4.Character               |   No Parse Method 
                          |
5.Boolena                 |   parseBoolean()
                          |
6.Short                   |   parseShort()
                          |
7.Byte                    |   parseByte()
                          |
8.Long                    |   parseLong()
                          |


